# /new resets the conversation. Turn 1 plants a token. After /new the
# model must NOT recall it, because its history was cleared. We assert
# the token is absent from the post-/new reply, then /quit.
#
# Note: we use expect_text on the *acknowledgement* token in turn 1 to
# prove the first turn landed, and a different deterministic anchor in
# turn 2 (the model is asked to literally type "fresh-OK") to prove
# the second turn ran. The recall failure is implicit: if /new failed
# to clear history, turn 2's reply would echo zag-ephemeral-XX.

spawn ./zig-out/bin/zag
wait_text /Welcome to zag/
wait_idle 500ms
send "Remember this token: zag-ephemeral-XX. Reply with just the word ack." <Enter>
wait_idle 20s
expect_text /ack/
send "/new" <Enter>
wait_idle 1s
send "Without referring to any prior conversation, reply with exactly the literal string: fresh-OK" <Enter>
wait_idle 20s
expect_text /fresh-OK/
snapshot final
send "/quit" <Enter>
wait_exit
